      "message": "1:CTS tests are failing:\nBug: 170072925   Broken test: android.hardware.input.cts.tests.GameviceGv186Test#testAllMotions on git_master on cf_x86_phone-userdebug at 6881927\nBug: 170126889   SC - CTS-on-GSI: android.hardware.input.cts.tests.RazerKishiTest#testAllMotions failure\n\n2: With CTS tests running on phone devices like coral which kernel is msm 4.14 it doesn\u0027t have the problem because the hid-input.c doesn\u0027t check the HID_QUIRK_INCREMENT_USAGE_ON_DUPLICATE, but the the common kernel does.\n\n3:We started to see these failures on git_master/cf_x86_phone-userdebug because of the kernel behavior,  I didn\u0027t say we are not seeing on android11-5.4 branch, it there is a build with it the CTS will also fail on that target. The issues were found on git_master/cf_x86_phone-userdebug which uses 5.4 kernel, so this would fix the CTS test failure on cf_x86_phone-userdebug target.",
